.Dd February 19, 2026
.Dt ELFOBJ_ARCHITECTURE 7
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm libelfobj architecture
.Nd design and architecture of the ELF object handling library
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This document describes the internal architecture and design principles
of the
.Nm libelfobj
library, a lightweight ELF object handling library designed for use in
toolchain components, debuggers, and the dynamic linker.
.Ss Design Goals
The library was designed with the following goals:
.Bl -tag -width "Embeddability"
.It Sy Simplicity
A clean, minimal API that covers common ELF manipulation tasks without
exposing unnecessary complexity.
.It Sy Safety
Robust handling of malformed input, suitable for processing untrusted
ELF files.
.It Sy Portability
No dependencies on system-specific ELF headers or libraries.
.It Sy Embeddability
Suitable for inclusion in other projects with minimal build requirements.
.It Sy Extensibility
Plugin-based architecture for supporting new target architectures.
.El
.Ss Object Model
The library's object model mirrors the ELF format structure:
.Bd -literal
elfobj_t (ELF Object)
    |
    +-- elf_section_t[] (Sections)
    |       |
    |       +-- Section data (bytes)
    |       +-- elf_reloc_t[] (Relocations)
    |
    +-- elf_symbol_t[] (Symbols)
    |
    +-- elf_reloc_t[] (Global relocation list)
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "elf_reloc_t"
.It Vt elfobj_t
Represents an entire ELF file.
Contains the ELF header, section table, symbol table, and relocation
information.
.It Vt elf_section_t
Represents an ELF section.
Contains section header information and optional data.
.It Vt elf_symbol_t
Represents an ELF symbol.
Contains symbol name, value, size, binding, type, and other attributes.
.It Vt elf_reloc_t
Represents an ELF relocation.
Contains the target section, offset, symbol reference, type, and addend.
.El
.Ss Internal Structure
The library is organized into the following modules:
.Bl -tag -width "elf_write.c"
.It Pa elf_read.c
ELF parsing and object construction from files or memory.
.It Pa elf_write.c
ELF serialization and file writing.
.It Pa elf_sections.c
Section management (add, find, set data).
.It Pa elf_symbols.c
Symbol management (add, find, query).
.It Pa elf_reloc.c
Relocation management and backend registration.
.It Pa elf_link.c
Object linking and merging.
.It Pa elf_validate.c
Structural validation and diagnostics.
.It Pa elf_hash.c
SYSV and GNU hash function implementations.
.It Pa elf_util.c
Utility functions (memory allocation, bounds checking, I/O).
.It Pa elf_layout.c
Section layout and offset computation.
.It Pa elf_strtab.c
String table construction and management.
.El
.Ss Memory Management
The library uses a consistent memory ownership model:
.Bl -tag -width "Caller-Owned"
.It Sy Library-Owned
Memory allocated by the library for internal use.
Freed automatically when the parent object is closed.
Examples: section data, symbol names, relocation entries.
.It Sy Caller-Owned
Memory allocated by the library for the caller.
Must be freed by the caller using
.Xr free 3 .
Examples: diagnostic strings from
.Fn elf_validate .
.It Sy Caller-Provided
Memory provided by the caller to the library.
The library makes copies; caller retains ownership.
Examples: section data passed to
.Fn elf_section_set_data .
.El
.Pp
All library allocations use internal wrappers around
.Xr malloc 3
and
.Xr free 3
to ensure consistent behavior and enable future memory tracking.
.Ss Error Handling
The library uses a two-level error reporting system:
.Bl -enum
.It
Function return codes
.Pq Vt elf_err_t
indicate success or failure.
.It
Object-specific error state stores detailed error messages.
.El
.Pp
Error codes are defined in the
.Vt elf_err_t
enumeration:
.Bl -column "ELF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED" "Description"
.It Sy Code Ta Sy Description
.It Dv ELF_OK Ta Success
.It Dv ELF_ERR_IO Ta Input/output error
.It Dv ELF_ERR_FORMAT Ta Invalid ELF format
.It Dv ELF_ERR_RELOC Ta Relocation error
.It Dv ELF_ERR_OOM Ta Out of memory
.It Dv ELF_ERR_BOUNDS Ta Bounds check failure
.It Dv ELF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED Ta Feature not supported
.It Dv ELF_ERR_STATE Ta Invalid object state
.It Dv ELF_ERR_NOTFOUND Ta Entity not found
.El
.Pp
Use
.Fn elf_errstr
to convert error codes to human-readable strings.
.Ss Backend Plugin Architecture
Relocation processing is delegated to architecture-specific backends:
.Bd -literal
Application
    |
    v
libelfobj Core
    |
    +-- Backend: i386
    +-- Backend: x86-64
    +-- Backend: ARM
    +-- Backend: Custom (user-registered)
.Ed
.Pp
Each backend implements:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fn apply_reloc :
Compute relocation values.
.It
.Fn reloc_size :
Query relocation target size.
.It
.Fn is_pc_relative :
Determine if relocation is PC-relative.
.El
.Pp
Backends are registered globally and persist for the process lifetime.
See
.Xr elf_backend 3
for details.
.Ss Thread Safety Model
The library provides the following thread-safety guarantees:
.Bl -tag -width "Object Operations"
.It Sy Global Operations
.Fn elf_errstr
and
.Fn elf_register_reloc_backend
are thread-safe.
.It Sy Object Operations
All functions operating on the same
.Vt elfobj_t
handle are NOT thread-safe.
Callers must synchronize concurrent access.
.It Sy Independent Objects
Different
.Vt elfobj_t
handles may be used concurrently without synchronization.
.El
.Pp
This model allows:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Parallel processing of multiple ELF files.
.It
Thread-safe error message lookup.
.It
Simple integration without complex locking.
.El
.Ss Validation and Security
The validation subsystem provides:
.Bl -tag -width "Diagnostic Output"
.It Sy Bounds Checking
All offsets and sizes are validated before use.
.It Sy Overflow Detection
Arithmetic operations are checked for overflow.
.It Sy Format Validation
ELF structures are checked for consistency.
.It Sy Diagnostic Output
Detailed error messages for debugging.
.El
.Pp
These features make the library suitable for processing untrusted input.
See
.Xr elf_validate 3
for security considerations.
.Ss Linking Pipeline
The linking process follows these phases:
.Bd -literal
Input Objects
    |
    v
+-------------------+
| Compatibility     |  Check architecture, class, endianness
+-------------------+
    |
    v
+-------------------+
| Section Merge     |  Concatenate same-named sections
+-------------------+
    |
    v
+-------------------+
| Symbol Resolution |  Merge symbol tables, resolve references
+-------------------+
    |
    v
+-------------------+
| Relocation Fixup  |  Adjust offsets and symbol indices
+-------------------+
    |
    v
Output Object
.Ed
.Pp
See
.Xr elf_link 3
for limitations and future enhancements.
.Ss ABI Stability
The library maintains a stable ABI for:
.Bl -bullet
.It
All public function signatures.
.It
Enumeration values and layouts.
.It
Backend structure layout.
.El
.Pp
The following are NOT part of the stable ABI:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Opaque type layouts
.Pq Vt elfobj_t , Vt elf_section_t , etc.
.It
Private functions and macros.
.It
Internal data structures.
.El
.Pp
Programs using only the public API will remain compatible with
future library versions.
.Ss Future Directions
Planned enhancements include:
.Bl -tag -width "Program Headers"
.It Sy Program Headers
Support for executable and shared library creation.
.It Sy Dynamic Linking
Generation of dynamic symbol tables, hash tables, and relocation tables.
.It Sy Archive Support
Direct reading and extraction from
.Pa .a
archive files.
.It Sy Relaxation
Linker relaxation optimization for code size reduction.
.It Sy Section GC
Garbage collection of unreferenced sections.
.It Sy LTO Support
Link-time optimization metadata handling.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "include/elfobj.h"
.It Pa include/elfobj.h
Public API header.
.It Pa usr.lib/elfobj/src/*.c
Implementation source files.
.It Pa usr.lib/elfobj/src/elf_private.h
Internal data structures and functions.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elfobj 3 ,
.Xr elf_section 3 ,
.Xr elf_symbol 3 ,
.Xr elf_reloc 3 ,
.Xr elf_link 3 ,
.Xr elf_validate 3 ,
.Xr elf_backend 3 ,
.Xr elf 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm libelfobj
library was created for the Substrate operating system to provide
a lightweight, embeddable ELF handling library.
It was designed to avoid the complexity and dependencies of existing
libraries like
.Nm libelf
and
.Nm libdwarf ,
while providing sufficient functionality for toolchain utilities,
debuggers, and the dynamic linker.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
The
.Nm libelfobj
library was written by the Substrate project team.
.Sh BUGS
.Bl -bullet
.It
Program header support is incomplete.
.It
Dynamic linking structures are not generated.
.It
Archive file handling is not supported.
.It
Section garbage collection is not implemented.
.It
Symbol versioning support is incomplete.
.El
